// A `u16` handed to a `*const u16` parameter of a FREE function. The reference
// refuses it: its one auto-ref sits on the method call path, not here.
//
// The port used to accept this, because it kept the rule in the coercion that
// reads the free-function signature table - the rule was pinned to a TABLE where
// the reference pins it to a PATH, so it fired exactly where it should not and
// stayed silent exactly where it should.
fn takes(p: *const u16) -> int { return 0; }
fn main() { let x: u16 = 5 as u16; println(takes(x)); }
